cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "pcf-edge-lean: A machine-checked Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the M9 Newton-edge algebraic core for polynomial continued fractions (conditional on H_edge)"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the purely algebraic / finitary core of
  the M9 Newton-edge lemma for polynomial continued fractions (PCFs) with
  unit numerator and partial denominator b(n) = sum_{k=0}^d beta_k n^k. Four
  theorems are PROVEN with the clean axiom cone {propext, Classical.choice,
  Quot.sound} and zero sorry: shift-invariance of the leading coefficient
  ([theta^d] b(theta+1) = beta_d), the closed form of the slope-1/d edge
  polynomial chi_d(c) = 1 + (-1)^(d+1)(beta_d/d^d)c^d, the affine-reindexing
  leading-coefficient law (gamma-free), and the xi0 = d/beta_d^{1/d}
  covariance xi0(b o phi) = alpha^{-1} xi0(b). The analytic edge => Borel
  singularity radius step (Wasow section 19 / Birkhoff-Trjitzinsky) is OUT OF
  SCOPE and is encoded as an explicit, unproved axiom H_edge; the Borel-radius
  covariance end statement is therefore PROVEN CONDITIONAL on H_edge, with the
  hypothesis visible in its axiom cone by design.
